# Dotfiles

## Linux and WSL

git clone https://github.com/bader/dotfiles.git ~/.dotfiles
cd ~/.dotfiles
./install

The installer links the Neovim configuration and installs Neovim when needed:
- Ubuntu: the latest upstream x86_64 release under `~/.local/bin`.
- Omarchy: the distribution `neovim` package via `pacman`.

Start `nvim` once after installation to let `lazy.nvim` install its plugins.

On Windows, use a Linux distribution under WSL and run these commands from the
distribution's home directory, not from `/mnt/c`.

This repository contains config files for:
- Vim
- Neovim
- Zsh/Bash
- Midnight Commander
